WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:04.156
- [Joshua] Garden City is, it's an oasis.

00:00:04.156 --> 00:00:07.617
I hope it's what America becomes.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:09.258
- [Miguel] You'll find
a lot of people here

00:00:09.258 --> 00:00:12.008
that are willing to do hard work.

00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:16.860
They'll come in and
they'll sit down, unwind.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.366
Anyone can get their hair cut
here at Exclusive Barber shop

00:00:19.366 --> 00:00:22.033
but only the best can work here.

00:00:27.264 --> 00:00:29.251
- [Announcer] To see a glimpse
into the future of America,

00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:32.992
Modelo looks not to its
coast, but to its heart.

00:00:32.992 --> 00:00:34.189
It's there that we found

00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:36.109
the hard-working community of Garden City,

00:00:36.109 --> 00:00:40.317
a place where people come
together to make a better life.

00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:42.157
- Of the barbershops today,

00:00:42.157 --> 00:00:45.576
are missing a whole lot
of what it used to be,

00:00:45.576 --> 00:00:47.715
where there was guys would come in,

00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:49.496
they socially connect.

00:00:49.496 --> 00:00:50.781
- The whole community comes in here,

00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:52.793
and they all get along.

00:00:52.793 --> 00:00:54.259
- [Joshua] Younger guys
listen to older guys,

00:00:54.259 --> 00:00:55.843
and older guys listen to younger guys.

00:00:55.843 --> 00:00:58.416
Ideas are exchanged, conversations happen.

00:00:58.416 --> 00:00:59.880
I mean that's what happens in here,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.960
and everybody seems to enjoy that.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.619
- It's just real fun to be here really.

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:06.221
- I mean there's so many different people

00:01:06.221 --> 00:01:07.445
that come in here,

00:01:07.445 --> 00:01:08.717
it's always interesting.

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.256
It's always a conversation

00:01:11.256 --> 00:01:13.080
from somebody from somewhere else.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.163
I really enjoy that part.

00:01:19.402 --> 00:01:23.069
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:38.341 --> 00:01:39.842
- [Carlos] Every time I get a chance to,

00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:42.435
I'm in the studio trying to do something.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.518
Make a noise.

00:01:45.352 --> 00:01:47.888
What I'm trying to work at
is get my name out there.

00:01:47.888 --> 00:01:50.218
I want the world to know my music,

00:01:50.218 --> 00:01:52.718
where I came from, my culture.

00:01:53.735 --> 00:01:56.560
- [James] You can trust each
other when you know each other.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.778
If you wanna know about Garden City,

00:01:58.778 --> 00:02:00.429
you read the newspaper.

00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:03.875
When you read the newspaper,
you see my stories.

00:02:03.875 --> 00:02:06.438
I'm willing to work past the 9-to-5,

00:02:06.438 --> 00:02:08.117
if I have to, to cover these stories,

00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:12.034
because it's important
to me and the community.

00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:20.298
- People working together
here in Garden City,

00:02:20.298 --> 00:02:24.357
the spirit comes from
just trust and respect.

00:02:24.357 --> 00:02:25.797
- People from all over the world

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:28.160
have kind of unified together

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.410
to form a really nice town.

00:02:31.461 --> 00:02:34.378
I believe we all want
our children to grow up

00:02:34.378 --> 00:02:36.072
better than what we did,

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:38.562
and the best way for that is to

00:02:38.562 --> 00:02:40.960
live peacefully amongst each other.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.127
I mean that's, that's what I
think we could learn from it.

